## Contract first

<!-- GEN: Where the contract lives on each side (e.g. Pydantic schemas ↔ lib/types.ts, OpenAPI → generated types). -->
- BE and FE agree on the API contract ({{be_contract_location}} ↔ {{fe_contract_location}}) before coding.
- One concept, one name across the boundary: {{shared_terms}}.
- Status codes, nulls, pagination and date formats are contract concerns; FE never invents a missing API or turns a failure into an empty success.

## Execution order

Finish and test the BE API before implementing the FE client.

## Authorization

- Backend guards ({{be_guard_location}}) are the authority.
- FE reads {{fe_capability_source}} to show/hide actions; this is UX only. FE handles 401/403 explicitly and never compares role strings.

